                <head>141. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In a memorandum to the Secretary, November 27, Assistant Secretary of State
                    Elbrick had indicated that the Italian Embassy had informed the Department of
                    State that Foreign Minister Giuseppe Pella wished to meet with Dulles as a form
                    of preliminary consultation prior to the NATO Heads of Government Meeting in
                    Paris (December 16–19). Dulles approved Elbrick’s recommendation that he meet
                    with Pella. (Department of State, Central Files, 765.13/11–2757)</p>
                <p>The memoranda of conversation covering the meetings in Washington among Dulles,
                    Pella, and their advisers on December 6 indicate that questions pertaining to
                    NATO, the Middle East, and disarmament were discussed. (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ibid.,</hi> Secretary’s Memoranda of Conversation: Lot 64 D199)</p>
            </div>
